# Who reviews what in the guide.
#
# A page about how a team works is reviewed by that team. Adding a
# section here is the easiest way to get the right people onto a pull
# request automatically, rather than remembering to tag them.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, and a match replaces the owners rather
# than adding to them. So the order below goes broad to narrow: the
# whole repo, then whole areas, then the sections a single team runs.
#
# @rladies/website keeps everything not claimed further down - layouts,
# config, the theme - and CI covers what they used to check by eye:
# check-build fails on a Hugo error, link-check catches broken links,
# i18n-check reports missing translations, alt-text-check looks at
# images, and Netlify posts a preview.

*                                       @rladies/website

# Areas that are global team business generally. Anything here without
# a more specific owner below goes to the whole global team.
content/global-team/                    @rladies/global
content/about/                          @rladies/global
content/community/                      @rladies/global
content/coordination/                   @rladies/global
content/ally/                           @rladies/global
content/acknowledgements/               @rladies/global

